,[1.569,0.38994172044171316],[1.6710000000000003,0.2707723472555546],[1.7715000000000005,0.1909576137929894],[1.8719999999999999,0.136033664842287],[2.0040000000000004,0.08846110795112873],[2.1390000000000002,0.05795734987488788],[2.2755,0.0384436362945639],[2.415,0.025700370622863518],[2.5575,0.017318764132834532],[2.7015000000000002,0.011810625511763725],[2.8485000000000005,0.008116354946507226],[3.0,0.0056]]}],"marks":[],"legend":[["line","K","the neutral bridge"],["line","reference","the charged bridge with no mass"]],"caption":["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the neutral and massless charged bridges against $u$, the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$. The horizontal coordinate is $u/\\sqrt{r_s}$ for the neutral bridge and $u/r_q$ for the charged one, and the vertical coordinate is $K r_s^4$ and $K r_q^4$, respectively. Negative and positive $u$ cover the two sheets, with the bridge at $u = 0$.","For the neutral bridge $r = r_s + u^2$ and $K = 12r_s^2/r^6$. For the charged bridge $r^2 = u^2 + r_q^2$ and $K = 56r_q^4/r^8$. From either sheet $K$ tends to $12/r_s^4$ at the neutral bridge and $56/r_q^4$ at the charged one. These are the limits from $u \\ne 0$; the metric is degenerate at $u = 0$. On each sheet the Ricci scalar vanishes."],"settings":"$r_s = 1$ for the neutral bridge, $r_q = 1$ and zero mass for the charged one, each radius the unit of length in its curve. We draw $|u| \\le 2.2\\sqrt{r_s}$ for the neutral bridge and $|u| \\le 3r_q$ for the charged one.","clip":"We draw $K$ in inverse fourth powers of each bridge radius on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-4}$ to $10^2$; both curves lie wholly within the panel."}]}
